      "refersTo": "nav-item",
      "description": "Register-cover rail with icon links; current page on a raised navy step.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-rail\"><a class=\"ds-nav ds-nav-on\" href=\"#\" aria-current=\"page\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"7\" height=\"7\" rx=\"1\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"14\" width=\"7\" height=\"7\" rx=\"1\"/><path d=\"M14 4h7M14 9h7M14 15h7M14 20h7\"/></svg>Overview</a><a class=\"ds-nav\" href=\"#\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2\"/><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"7\" r=\"4\"/><path d=\"M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75\"/></svg>People</a></nav>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#f3f5f9;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#14171f;--ink-2:#4b5263;--ink-3:#626a7b;--rule:#e2e6ee;--rule-strong:#c9d0dc;--rail:#1b2c57;--rail-ink:#eef2fb;--rail-ink-2:#aebbd9;--rail-hover:#22376a;--rail-active:#2b4384;--blue:#256abf;--blue-wash:#eaf2fd;--red:#c4373a;--mark-0:#e6eaf1;--slot-line:#b9c1cf;--mark-1:#86b6ef;--mark-2:#3987e5;--mark-3:#1c5cab;--mark-4:#0d366b;}.ds-rail{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;width:216px;padding:12px;background:var(--rail);font-family:'Hanken Grotesk',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:8px 12px;border-radius:8px;font-size:.9375rem;color:var(--rail-ink-2);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color .15s,color .15s}.ds-nav:hover{background:var(--rail-hover);color:var(--rail-ink)}.ds-nav:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #6da7ec;outline-offset:2px}.ds-nav-on,.ds-nav-on:hover{background:var(--rail-active);color:var(--rail-ink)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sheet",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "sheet",
      "description": "Flat white container with a hairline border and a ruled table head; no shadow.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-sheet\"><h2 class=\"ds-title\">People to check on</h2><div class=\"ds-head\">Person</div><div class=\"ds-row\">Maya Chen</div><div class=\"ds-row\">Tom Okafor</div></section>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#f3f5f9;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#14171f;--ink-2:#4b5263;--ink-3:#626a7b;--rule:#e2e6ee;--rule-strong:#c9d0dc;--rail:#1b2c57;--rail-ink:#eef2fb;--rail-ink-2:#aebbd9;--rail-hover:#22376a;--rail-active:#2b4384;--blue:#256abf;--blue-wash:#eaf2fd;--red:#c4373a;--mark-0:#e6eaf1;--slot-line:#b9c1cf;--mark-1:#86b6ef;--mark-2:#3987e5;--mark-3:#1c5cab;--mark-4:#0d366b;}.ds-sheet{width:360px;background:var(--sheet);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;color:var(--ink);font-family:'Hanken Grotesk',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-title{margin:0;padding:20px 20px 16px;font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em}.ds-head{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Hanken Grotesk',sans-serif;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8125rem;line-height:1;color:var(--ink-3);padding:10px 20px;border-top:1px solid var(--rule-strong);border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule-strong)}.ds-row{padding:12px 20px;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.ds-row:last-child{border-bottom:0}.ds-row:hover{background:rgb(243 245 249 / .6)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Register Strip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "register-mark",
      "description": "Signature: one rounded-square mark per week on the shared ink ramp, with an open slot before joining and a hover readout.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-strip\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"Watched in 9 of the last 12 weeks\"><span class=\"ds-mark ds-slot\" style=\"--i:0\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-0);--i:1\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-1);--i:2\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-2);--i:3\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-2);--i:4\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-3);--i:5\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-4);--i:6\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-3);--i:7\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-2);--i:8\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-1);--i:9\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-0);--i:10\"></span><span class=\"ds-mark\" style=\"background:var(--mark-2);--i:11\"></span><div class=\"ds-tip\" role=\"tooltip\"><p class=\"ds-tip-d\">3 Nov – 9 Nov</p><p class=\"ds-tip-v\">7 plays · 5.5 h</p><p class=\"ds-tip-x\">Mostly Severance</p></div></div>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#f3f5f9;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#14171f;--ink-2:#4b5263;--ink-3:#626a7b;--rule:#e2e6ee;--rule-strong:#c9d0dc;--rail:#1b2c57;--rail-ink:#eef2fb;--rail-ink-2:#aebbd9;--rail-hover:#22376a;--rail-active:#2b4384;--blue:#256abf;--blue-wash:#eaf2fd;--red:#c4373a;--mark-0:#e6eaf1;--slot-line:#b9c1cf;--mark-1:#86b6ef;--mark-2:#3987e5;--mark-3:#1c5cab;--mark-4:#0d366b;}@keyframes ds-ink{from{opacity:.45;transform:scale(.55)}to{opacity:1;transform:scale(1)}}.ds-strip{position:relative;display:inline-flex;gap:3px;margin-top:84px;font-family:'Hanken Grotesk',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;border-radius:4px}.ds-strip:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--blue);outline-offset:2px}.ds-mark{display:block;width:13px;height:13px;border-radius:3px;animation:ds-ink 420ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both}.ds-mark:nth-child(n){animation-delay:calc(var(--i,0)*18ms)}.ds-mark:hover{outline:2px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:1px}.ds-slot{background:transparent;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--slot-line)}.ds-tip{position:absolute;bottom:100%;left:60%;transform:translateX(-50%);margin-bottom:8px;width:max-content;background:var(--sheet);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:8px;padding:8px 12px;font-size:.875rem;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgb(20 23 31 / .04),0 6px 18px -8px rgb(20 23 31 / .12)}.ds-tip p{margin:0}.ds-tip-d{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Hanken Grotesk',sans-serif;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8125rem;line-height:1;color:var(--ink-3)}.ds-tip-v{margin-top:4px!important;font-weight:500;color:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-tip-x{color:var(--ink-2)}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-mark{animation:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status Marks",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "register-mark",
      "description": "The one state vocabulary: filled, half, outline, dotted, dashed, struck, each with a plain label.",
      "html": "<ul class=\"ds-status\"><li><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><rect x=\".75\" y=\".75\" width=\"10.5\" height=\"10.5\" rx=\"2.9\" fill=\"var(--mark-3)\" stroke=\"var(--mark-3)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></svg>Active</li><li><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><rect x=\".75\" y=\".75\" width=\"10.5\" height=\"10.5\" rx=\"2.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--mark-2)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\".75\" y=\".75\" width=\"5.25\" height=\"10.5\" rx=\"2.9\" fill=\"var(--mark-2)\"/><rect x=\"3.1\" y=\".75\" width=\"2.9\" height=\"10.5\" fill=\"var(--mark-2)\"/></svg>Slowing down</li><li><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><rect x=\".75\" y=\".75\" width=\"10.5\" height=\"10.5\" rx=\"2.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--mark-2)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></svg>Gone quiet</li><li><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><rect x=\".75\" y=\".75\" width=\"10.5\" height=\"10.5\" rx=\"2.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--ink-3)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg>Never watched</li><li><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><rect x=\".75\" y=\".75\" width=\"10.5\" height=\"10.5\" rx=\"2.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--mark-2)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/></svg>Invite pending</li><li><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><rect x=\".75\" y=\".75\" width=\"10.5\" height=\"10.5\" rx=\"2.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--ink-3)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M2.64 9.36 9.36 2.64\" stroke=\"var(--ink-3)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg>Removed</li><li><span class=\"ds-slotkey\"></span>Not yet joined</li></ul>",
      "css": ":host{--paper:#f3f5f9;--sheet:#fff;--ink:#14171f;--ink-2:#4b5263;--ink-3:#626a7b;--rule:#e2e6ee;--rule-strong:#c9d0dc;--rail:#1b2c57;--rail-ink:#eef2fb;--rail-ink-2:#aebbd9;--rail-hover:#22376a;--rail-active:#2b4384;--blue:#256abf;--blue-wash:#eaf2fd;--red:#c4373a;--mark-0:#e6eaf1;--slot-line:#b9c1cf;--mark-1:#86b6ef;--mark-2:#3987e5;--mark-3:#1c5cab;--mark-4:#0d366b;}.ds-status{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:8px;font-family:'Hanken Grotesk',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.875rem;color:var(--ink-2)}.ds-status li{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}.ds-slotkey{display:block;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--slot-line)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Attendance Register",
    "overview": "Playbill's admin UI is a ruled register on cool paper-white, bound under a deep register-cover blue rail. Every person is a row and every week is a mark, so who has been around and who has drifted reads at a glance. The register strip, one square mark per week on one shared weekly scale, is the world's repeated form: it appears at 12 weeks on Overview and People, at 52 weeks (four 13-week quarters) on a person's page, as the peak-hours grid, and even as the two-row wordmark beside the product name.\n\nThe surface is calm and dense, the density of a well-kept ledger rather than a dashboard. Numbers live in sentences (\"12 of 41 people watched in the last 7 days\") and in ruled tables, never in stat tiles. Sheets are flat white with hairline rules; column heads are condensed printed caps; names and prose are set in a warm humanist grotesk. Colour is almost entirely one blue ink, stepped by how much someone watched; red ink is held back for the owner. In dark mode the paper becomes a blue-black, the rail deepens, and the ink ramp inverts so the strongest week is still the most visible mark.\n\nMotion has one gesture: when the range changes, marks ink in from left to right (420ms, 18ms stagger per mark), and it is switched off under reduced motion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One shared weekly scale, drawn as rounded square marks in an ordinal blue ramp, everywhere attendance appears.",
      "One state-mark vocabulary for status: filled, half, outline, dotted, dashed, struck, plus the open \"not yet joined\" slot.",
      "Flat white sheets with hairline borders on a cool grey paper; shadow only on floating tooltips.",
      "Condensed uppercase caps for column heads and tick labels; humanist grotesk for everything a person reads.",
      "Tabular figures for every number, so columns of counts and hours align like a ledger.",
      "Red only where the owner has to act."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Ink Rule",
        "body": "Attendance and volume are only ever drawn in the `mark-0` to `mark-4` ramp. No second hue, no gradient, no categorical palette; a mark's darkness is its quantity.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Owner's Red Rule",
        "body": "Red appears only where the owner must act: a removal or warning awaiting their decision, or something broken they must fix. It is never decoration, never a trend colour, never an \"inactive\" signal. A screen with nothing for the owner to do has no red on it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shared Scale Rule",
        "body": "The four hour bands (under 1 h, 1-3 h, 3-8 h, 8 h+) mean the same thing on every page, and every register carries its key.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ledger Figures Rule",
        "body": "Every number is set in tabular figures (the `num` utility, `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`): headline counts, range segments, filter counts, plays, hours, dates, axis labels.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Printed Head Rule",
        "body": "Condensed caps are for structural labels that sit over or beside data (column heads, ticks, tooltip date lines). Never for sentences, names, buttons or headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Border-Not-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Sheets are bordered, never shadowed. A shadow means \"this is floating over the page, briefly\"; only tooltips earn it.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** draw any per-week or per-hour quantity as rounded-square marks in the `mark-0` to `mark-4` ramp, on the shared hour bands, with a key.",
      "**Do** state a person's segment with the status-mark vocabulary (filled, half, outline, dotted, dashed, struck, open slot) plus a plain label.",
      "**Do** put numbers in sentences and ruled tables, and set every number with tabular figures.",
      "**Do** separate content with 1px `rule` hairlines and a `rule-strong` line around table heads.",
      "**Do** use `rail` navy for the single primary action and for selected states.",
      "**Do** keep column heads and ticks in Barlow Condensed caps at 0.8125rem / 0.06em, and everything else in Hanken Grotesk.",
      "**Do** honour reduced motion: the ink-in animation is the only motion and it switches off."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** build KPI stat tiles or big-number cards; the headline is a sentence.",
      "**Don't** use red for anything other than an owner decision or a failure the owner must fix.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second data hue or a categorical palette for attendance.",
      "**Don't** put a shadow on a sheet, card or panel; shadows are for tooltips only.",
      "**Don't** signal state by colour alone; the mark's shape must carry it.",
      "**Don't** set sentences, names or buttons in condensed caps."
    ]
  }
}